# Strategic Command WWII: War in Europe  (Steam appid 593030)
#
# First 32-bit title in this environment -- everything debugged so far was
# 64-bit Chromium. (It was described as "D3D9" for a while; it is not. It is
# SDL 1.2, and in any case the graphics API turned out to be irrelevant -- see
# below.)
#
# Installed in the shared library on S:, so it is not tied to this prefix and a
# per-game prefix later costs nothing. Note Steam creates a SteamLibrary/
# subfolder under whatever mount point you register, hence the path below.
#
# ⚠️ NEEDS A GAME-FILE FIX (2026-10-02): tools/fixes/vorbis-sse.sh install "<game dir>"
# The game's own vorbis.dll is x87-only (3013 x87 / 0 SSE) and it decodes whole
# music tracks on the main thread, so under Rosetta every transition froze the
# UI: Quit took 49 s, the first music was slow to start, menu -> map ~23 s.
# CrossOver is exactly as slow (Music/loop3.ogg: 51.66 s vs our 51.45 s), so
# it is the platform, not our runtime. With the SSE libvorbis build: decode
# 3.26 s, start ~5 s, Quit < 1 s (user-timed). Steam's "Verify integrity" or a
# game update restores the original -- re-run the install after either.

RUNTIME="winecx-26.3.0-sse-x86_64"
PREFIX="steam-winecx"

# The graphics backend is IRRELEVANT here and this is now settled, not assumed.
# The game dies in Wine's WoW64 32->64 transition thunk long before it draws
# anything, so no D3D/GL/ddraw code is ever reached -- which is why wined3d and
# DXVK produced identical symptoms. See docs/NEXT.md, "The WoW64 mode switch".
#
# Left at "none" as the honest baseline: DXVK's d3d9=n override cannot be in the
# path of an SDL 1.2 title (Wine's ddraw talks to wined3d directly and never
# loads d3d9.dll), and carrying it only added noise to every trace.
BACKEND="none"

# Launch through Steam rather than running the exe directly.
#
# Running SC3-WWII directly always exits 53: steam_api.dll re-launches the game
# via steam://run/<appid> and quits, and that hand-off goes through Wine's URL
# handler, which does not inherit our environment -- so the Steam it starts has
# no WINE_APPEND_ARGS and comes up black. -applaunch is the supported entry
# point: Steam owns the launch, and because gamerun starts *this* process, the
# whole tree inherits the environment we want.
EXE='C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steam.exe'
WORKDIR="$PREFIXES_DIR/steam-winecx/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Steam"

ARGS="-applaunch 593030"

PROFILE_ENV=(
    WINEDEBUG=-all
)

# Nothing forced yet. Note bin/gamerun sets WINE_APPEND_ARGS for every launch:
# a Steam game still needs it, because steam_api.dll will start the client and
# the overlay is CEF -- launching without it leaves a black Steam window.
WINEDLLOVERRIDES=""
